Applies on top of tools/no-float-doubleword.patch to decompals/mips-binutils-2.6
(commit 54514de, tag v0.3). Makes the rebuilt assembler behave like the one that
built the ROM. KMC maps -mips3 to ISA 2 internally, so every ISA-gated hazard rule
has to be read with that in mind:
  - -g2 keeps hazard nops conditional (mips_optimize 1) instead of unconditional;
  - no nop after mtc1/ctc1 before a use (the VR4300 interlocks them);
  - no nop after mfc1/cfc1 before a use or before a .set noreorder block
    (GCC's filled `jal` right after `mfc1 $a0` is common);
  - exactly one nop after an FP compare when a pseudo-op follows, not two;
  - no nop when one instruction already separates an FP compare from the
    pseudo-op before its branch (`c.lt.s; addiu; .set noreorder; bc1t`);
  - the sym($reg) load macro always uses $at as its scratch register;
  - no HI/LO hazard nops at a `.set noreorder` directive: GCC's filled
    `bnez`/`j` right after `mfhi`/`mflo` follows at once (the padding before
    a `div`/`mult` macro stays: `mfhi; lhu; nop; div` is in the ROM);
  - the VR4300 mulmul fix (gas/input-file.c, on by default) no longer treats a
    line starting in column 0 (a label) as a float multiply: the ROM pads only
    `mul.s`/`mul.d` followed by another `mul*`, so the Makefile drops
    `--vr4300mul-off` (60 `mul; nop; mul` sites in the ROM);
  - `--fp-move-nops` (gas/as.c) pads mtc1/mfc1 and the two-instruction FP
    compare hazard like an unpatched assembler at ISA 1, for the libultra
    unit only (its objects came with those nops): src/18020_C0800.o gets
    `-Wa,--fp-move-nops` in the Makefile;
  - a float multiply never sits in a branch delay slot (0 cases in the ROM,
    45 in our build): in a .set noreorder block the slot's mul.s/mul.d is
    moved in front of the branch and the slot gets a nop; in reorder mode
    one is never swapped in. Not under --fp-move-nops (the libultra unit's
    assembler did fill slots with multiplies);
  - an FP compare followed by a label or directive is padded only when the
    next instruction reads the condition code (`c.eq.s; j` has no nop in
    the ROM; `c.lt.s; .L: nop; bc1t` keeps its nop after the label);
  - a label defined before a hazard nop stays in front of it (`c.lt.s; .L: nop;
    bc1t`, 30 times in the ROM, never the moved form): neither append_insn nor
    mips_emit_delays moves insn_label past the nops it inserts.
  - a multiply after a float multiply is padded even when a branch without
    link and its delay-slot nop sit between them (`mul.s; j .L; nop; nop;
    mul.s` 10 times and `mul.s; bc1fl .L; nop; nop; mul.s` 9 times in the ROM,
    never without the second nop): the text-level fix cannot see through the
    branch, so append_insn checks the three emitted words before a mul*; when
    the second multiply is moved out of the next branch's delay slot, the nop
    goes in front of it (nop, mul, branch, nop; a label before the branch stays
    on the nop). Not under --fp-move-nops;
